      "started_at": "2026-11-05T16:03:59.832049+00:00",
      "result": {
        "reply_text": "I understand you are trying to recover unpaid wages from a private shop in Kanpur and have already spoken to your manager without success. Please keep your attendance screenshots and bank statements in a safe place as these are important records of your employment and payment history.\n\nUnder the law, employers must fix a wage period that does not exceed one month and pay wages within the prescribed time. If wages are not paid, they can be recovered through the authority appointed by the government to hear such claims. Courts generally do not entertain separate civil suits for claims that can be recovered through this specific legal process.\n\n1. Continue to keep a record of all your communications with the manager regarding the unpaid salary. 2. You may contact the Uttar Pradesh State Legal Services Authority for guidance on how to proceed with your claim. They can be reached at their toll-free helpline number or through their office in Lucknow.\n\nYou should consider speaking with a lawyer if you are unable to resolve the matter through the relevant government authority or if you need help filing a formal claim for your unpaid wages.\n\nDo you have an appointment letter or a salary slip from your employer? These documents can be very helpful in proving your employment and the amount of wages due.\n\nSource: Uttar Pradesh Dookan Aur Vanijya Adhishthan Adhiniyam, 1962, section 13\nSource: Code on Wages, 2019, section 45\nSource: Code on Wages, 2019, section 57\n\nNote: Payment of Wages Act, 1936 is no longer in force, so I do not use it.\n\nWhat I could not verify:\n- The specific procedure for filing a claim under the Payment of Wages Act, 1936, as referenced in the UP Act.\n- The exact prescribed time limit for payment of wages in UP.\n\nThis is legal information, not legal advice.",
